#: manual/conformance/bin_float.md:1
msgid "`bin_float` Conformance"
msgstr "`bin_float` 一致性说明"

#: manual/conformance/bin_float.md:3
msgid "This page records the `0.8.0` binary floating-point semantic and test boundary. It is evidence for a stated, finite corpus; it is not a proof that any implementation can be correct for every real input."
msgstr "本文记录 `0.8.0` 二进制浮点语义与验证边界。有限测试全部通过是声明范围内的证据，不是对所有实数输入的形式化证明。"

#: manual/conformance/bin_float.md:7
msgid "Normative And Research Sources"
msgstr "标准、论文与参考实现"

#: manual/conformance/bin_float.md:9
msgid "IEEE, *IEEE Standard for Floating-Point Arithmetic*, IEEE 754-2019: interchange formats, rounding-direction attributes, NaNs/infinities/signed zeros, exceptions, and tininess detection."
msgstr "IEEE 754-2019：interchange format、舍入方向、带符号零、NaN、异常标志与 before/after rounding 的 tininess 语义。"

#: manual/conformance/bin_float.md:12
msgid "S. Fousse, G. Hanrot, V. Lefèvre, P. Pélissier, and P. Zimmermann, [MPFR: A Multiple-Precision Binary Floating-Point Library with Correct Rounding](https://doi.org/10.1145/1236463.1236468), ACM TOMS 33(2), 2007. MPFR supplies the exact-result-then-one-rounding model used for arbitrary precisions."
msgstr "Fousse、Hanrot、Lefèvre、Pélissier、Zimmermann， [MPFR: A Multiple-Precision Binary Floating-Point Library with Correct Rounding](https://doi.org/10.1145/1236463.1236468)， ACM TOMS 33(2), 2007：任意精度的“精确结果、仅一次舍入”模型。"

#: manual/conformance/bin_float.md:16
#, fuzzy
msgid "John Hauser's Berkeley [SoftFloat](https://www.jhauser.us/arithmetic/SoftFloat.html) and [TestFloat](https://www.jhauser.us/arithmetic/TestFloat.html), release 3e, provide the independently generated IEEE result/flag vectors."
msgstr "Berkeley SoftFloat/TestFloat 3e：独立产生 IEEE 结果位与异常标志的参考实现和测试向量。"

#: manual/conformance/bin_float.md:20
msgid "Mathematical Model"
msgstr "数学语义与算法"

#: manual/conformance/bin_float.md:22
#, fuzzy
msgid "A finite nonzero `BinFloat` denotes the dyadic real"
msgstr "有限非零值表示 dyadic 实数"

#: manual/conformance/bin_float.md:24
msgid "`(-1)^negative * coefficient * 2^exponent2`, where `coefficient` is a non-negative `BinCoeff`."
msgstr "`(-1)^negative * coefficient * 2^exponent2`，其中 `coefficient` 是非负的 `BinCoeff`。"

#: manual/conformance/bin_float.md:27
#, fuzzy
msgid "The finite coefficient is normalized by removing factors of two, while the sign of zero remains observable. Infinity, qNaN, sNaN, NaN payload, and NaN sign are explicit states rather than sentinel finite values."
msgstr "非零 coefficient 会移除 2 因子以规范化；`+0` 与 `-0` 不会合并。无穷、qNaN、 sNaN、NaN 符号及 payload 都是显式状态。"

#: manual/conformance/bin_float.md:31
msgid "For `add_ctx`, `sub_ctx`, `mul_ctx`, `div_ctx`, `sqrt_ctx`, and `pow_int_ctx`:"
msgstr "`add_ctx`、`sub_ctx`、`mul_ctx`、`div_ctx`、`sqrt_ctx` 与 `pow_int_ctx` 的顺序固定为：先处理 IEEE 特殊值；在 dyadic/有理数或平方根界上计算精确数学结果；按目标精度和方向仅舍入一次；最后做指数范围/subnormal 量化，并从该过程导出五个 IEEE 标志。实现不会根据测试 ID、测试数值或向量格式选择分支。"

#: manual/conformance/bin_float.md:33
msgid "IEEE special cases are resolved before finite arithmetic."
msgstr ""

#: manual/conformance/bin_float.md:34
msgid "Finite addition, subtraction, and multiplication use their exact dyadic result; division uses an exact integer quotient/remainder decision; square root brackets the exact real root with integer-square-root bounds."
msgstr ""

#: manual/conformance/bin_float.md:37
msgid "The exact result is rounded once to the requested precision and rounding direction, then exponent-range/subnormal quantization is applied."
msgstr ""

#: manual/conformance/bin_float.md:39
msgid "The returned `BinaryFlags` is derived from that mathematical result: inexact, underflow, overflow, division-by-zero, and invalid-operation."
msgstr ""

#: manual/conformance/bin_float.md:42
msgid "This order matters. For example, binary16 `0x0400 * 0x3BFF` produces `0x0400` with `inexact | underflow`; after-rounding tininess is determined from the precision-rounded unbounded value, not merely from the final normal interchange encoding."
msgstr "例如 binary16 `0x0400 * 0x3BFF` 的结果位为 `0x0400`，标志仍为 `inexact | underflow`。after-rounding tininess 依据目标精度、无界指数的舍入结果，而不能由最终 normal 编码倒推。"

#: manual/conformance/bin_float.md:47
msgid "No operation branches on test identifiers, test values, or corpus format. The corpus interpreter is an adapter around the public contextual operations."
msgstr ""

#: manual/conformance/bin_float.md:50
msgid "Interchange And Context"
msgstr "固定语料与结果"

#: manual/conformance/bin_float.md:52
msgid "`BinaryInterchange` decodes and encodes IEEE binary16, binary32, binary64, and binary128 bit patterns. `BinaryContext` carries precision, rounding direction, paired exponent limits, and before/after tininess detection. Encoding and contextual arithmetic both return status flags; ordinary operators use an unbounded nearest-even context and intentionally do not expose those flags."
msgstr ""

#: manual/conformance/bin_float.md:58
msgid "NaN comparisons in the TestFloat adapter are class-based only when an expected result is NaN. This is not a weakened finite-value comparison: non-NaN encoded bits and all exception bits must match exactly. It reflects IEEE's permitted choice of a newly generated NaN payload. The implementation itself preserves the selected input NaN's sign/payload and quiets signaling NaNs."
msgstr ""

