#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:1
msgid "`bin_float` Tutorial"
msgstr "`bin_float` 教程"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:3
#, fuzzy
msgid "Use `bin_float` when values are naturally dyadic, when precision must exceed a host `Float`/`Double`, or when binary16/32/64/128 rounding and status are part of the result. This tutorial targets `floating` 0.8.0; see [API](../api/bin_float.md) for the complete inventory and [Conformance](../conformance/bin_float.md) for the verified IEEE boundary."
msgstr "适用于天然 dyadic、超出 host Float/Double 精度，或 binary16/32/64/128 rounding/status 属于结果契约的场景。本页基于 0.8.0。"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:13
msgid "exact arbitrary-precision dyadic work"
msgstr "任意精度精确 dyadic"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:13
#, fuzzy
msgid "ordinary `BinFloat` constructors and methods"
msgstr "普通构造与方法"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:14
msgid "fixed precision/exponent/rounding with flags"
msgstr "固定 precision/exponent/rounding + flags"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:15
#, fuzzy
msgid "binary16/32/64/128 bits"
msgstr "固定位模式"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:16
msgid "observable elementary certification failure"
msgstr "可观察认证失败"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:17
msgid "short-circuit checked composition"
msgstr "首错即停组合"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:19
msgid "Construct Exact Dyadic Values"
msgstr "构造精确 Dyadic 值"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:21
#, fuzzy
msgid "`BinFloat::make` receives a non-negative coefficient, a power-of-two exponent, and a working precision. The sign is a separate argument."
msgstr "`make` 接收非负 coefficient、二进制 exponent 与工作 precision；sign 独立。Normalization 会把二因子移入 exponent："

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:37
msgid "Normalization removes powers of two from a nonzero coefficient:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:52
#, fuzzy
msgid "Use `from_int`/`from_bigint` for integers. Use `from_double` only when the host binary64 value itself is the source of truth; it cannot recover a decimal value that was rounded before the call."
msgstr "整数优先使用 `from_int/from_bigint`。只有 host binary64 本身是事实来源时才用 `from_double`；它不能恢复调用前已经丢失的十进制信息。"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:56
msgid "Use A Binary Context"
msgstr "使用 Binary Context"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:58
msgid "Ordinary operators use the values' working precision. Use a `BinaryContext` when a specific interchange-style format, rounding direction, exponent range, or tininess rule is required."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:86
msgid "Keep the value and flags together until the application has applied its status policy. For a multi-step calculation, combine flags explicitly:"
msgstr "需要指定格式、rounding、exponent 或 tininess 时使用 context："

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:95
#, fuzzy
msgid "Do not assume that an infinity or NaN means there is no result. IEEE operations often return a defined special value and a flag such as division-by-zero or invalid-operation."
msgstr "多步计算要显式 `combine` flags，并让 value/flags 一起跨过应用边界。Infinity/NaN 常是带 flag 的 defined result，不能自动当作“无结果”。"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:99
msgid "Decode And Encode Interchange Bits"
msgstr "解码与编码 Interchange Bits"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:101
msgid "Use `BinaryInterchange` for protocol or file bits. Do not decode binary16, binary32, or binary128 through a host `Double`."
msgstr "固定格式必须通过 `BinaryInterchange`，不要经 host `Double`："

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:117
msgid "For NaNs, inspect class, signaling state, sign, and payload according to the application's protocol. Ordinary `compare` is not a total order over NaNs."
msgstr "协议若区分 NaN sign/payload 或 signed zero，就应保留/检查对应位状态。普通 `compare` 不是 NaN total order。"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:120
#: manual/tutorial/decimal.md:128
msgid "Call Certified Elementary Functions"
msgstr "调用认证初等函数"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:122
msgid "The `try_*_ctx` family exposes certification failure instead of aborting. This is the recommended boundary when input size or range is untrusted."
msgstr "不可信或超大输入优先使用 `try_*_ctx`："

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:144
#, fuzzy
msgid "Use `exp_ctx`, `sin_ctx`, and similar convenience methods only when a certification failure is considered unrecoverable. Both families execute the same certified enclosure/refinement algorithm; the difference is error policy."
msgstr "`exp_ctx/sin_ctx` 等 convenience API 使用相同 certificate，只是把证明失败视为不可恢复。"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:148
msgid "Retune Working Precision Deliberately"
msgstr "有意调整工作精度"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:150
msgid "`with_precision` changes the represented value if discarded bits are nonzero. Always state the rounding direction at this boundary."
msgstr "`with_precision` 可能改变表示值，因此边界上必须指定 rounding："

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:166
msgid "`ulp()` reports spacing for the current finite representation. It is useful for representation analysis, but it is not a certified error bound for a sequence of operations."
msgstr "`ulp()` 是当前表示的 spacing，不是多步计算的认证 error bound。"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:170
msgid "Handle Special Values Explicitly"
msgstr "显式处理特殊值"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:172
#, fuzzy
msgid "Construct signed zero with `zero` / `negative_zero`."
msgstr "使用 `zero/negative_zero`、`quiet_nan/signaling_nan`；"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:173
msgid "Construct NaNs with `quiet_nan` / `signaling_nan` and inspect `nan_payload`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:174
msgid "Use `classify()` before an ordered comparison when NaN is possible."
msgstr "NaN 可能出现时，ordered comparison 前先 `classify()`；"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:175
msgid "Use contextual operations when invalid, overflow, underflow, or inexact status affects control flow."
msgstr "status 影响控制流时使用 context API；"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:177
msgid "Preserve interchange bits when a protocol distinguishes NaN payloads or signed zero."
msgstr "协议关心 payload/signed zero 时保留 interchange bits。"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:182
msgid "Pick one working precision at the algorithm boundary; avoid repeatedly shrinking and expanding values."
msgstr "在算法边界一次确定工作 precision，避免反复缩放。"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:184
#, fuzzy
msgid "Decode fixed formats with `BinaryInterchange`, calculate with one explicit `BinaryContext`, and encode once at the output boundary."
msgstr "固定格式用 interchange 解码，用一个 context 计算，最后一次编码。"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:186
msgid "Accumulate flags beside the value rather than discarding them after each operation."
msgstr "不要丢弃中间 flags。"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:188
msgid "Prefer `try_*_ctx` for elementary functions over untrusted or very large inputs."
msgstr "不可信 elementary input 使用 `try_*_ctx`。"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:190
msgid "Do not depend on coefficient limb layout, NTT thresholds, or target-specific dispatch; those are intentionally private."
msgstr "不依赖 limb layout、NTT threshold 或 target dispatch。"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:195
msgid "[Design](../design/bin_float.md) explains exact kernels, certified rounding, and tuning boundaries."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:197
msgid "[Conformance](../conformance/bin_float.md) lists the exact TestFloat/MPFR evidence."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float.md:198
msgid "[`bin_float_checked` tutorial](bin_float_checked.md) shows a closed `Result` pipeline when first-error short-circuiting is desired."
msgstr "[Design](../design/bin_float.md) 解释 kernel/certificate/tuning；[Conformance](../conformance/bin_float.md) 列出 TestFloat/MPFR 证据；[`bin_float_checked`](bin_float_checked.md) 展示 closed `Result` pipeline。"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float_checked.md:1
msgid "`bin_float_checked` Tutorial"
msgstr "`bin_float_checked` 教程"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float_checked.md:3
msgid "`BinFloatResult` keeps `Result[BinFloat, ArithmeticError]` inside a fluent pipeline. Use it when the first checked construction or arithmetic failure should stop every later step. It is not an IEEE flag accumulator."
msgstr "`BinFloatResult` 把 `Result[BinFloat, ArithmeticError]` 保留在 fluent pipeline 中。适用于首次构造/算术错误应停止后续步骤的场景；它不是 IEEE flag accumulator。"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float_checked.md:7
msgid "Build A Pipeline"
msgstr "构建 Pipeline"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float_checked.md:20
#, fuzzy
msgid "Keep the wrapper until the application boundary. Call `result()` once the caller is ready to handle `ArithmeticError`; use `is_ok`, `is_err`, or `error()` for branch decisions without extracting the value."
msgstr "保持 wrapper 到应用边界；用 `is_ok/is_err/error` 分支，准备处理错误时再 `result()`。"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float_checked.md:24
msgid "Understand First-Error Short-Circuiting"
msgstr "理解首错短路"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float_checked.md:26
msgid "Every transformation on an error is the identity. In a binary method, the left error wins before the right is evaluated as a numerical operand. This makes the pipeline deterministic but intentionally does not collect multiple errors."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float_checked.md:30
msgid "Use `map` for an infallible `BinFloat -> BinFloat` transformation. Use `bind` when the callback may return another `BinFloatResult`. `flat_map` is a deprecated alias; new code should use `bind`."
msgstr "错误上的每次 transformation 都是 identity；binary method 先保留 left error。它保证 deterministic first-error，但不会收集多个错误。`map` 用于 infallible transform， callback 也可能失败时用 `bind`；`flat_map` 已 deprecated。"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float_checked.md:45
msgid "Contextual Operations Do Not Retain Flags"
msgstr "Context 操作不保留 Flags"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float_checked.md:47
#, fuzzy
msgid "Methods such as `add_ctx` and `exp_ctx` retain certification/arithmetic failure in the wrapper, but `BinFloatResult` stores only the resulting value or error. If IEEE `BinaryFlags` are part of the contract, call the underlying `BinFloat::*_ctx` API and carry `(value, flags)` explicitly."
msgstr "`add_ctx/exp_ctx` 会保留 certification/arithmetic failure，但 wrapper 只保存 value/error。 IEEE `BinaryFlags` 属于契约时，应直接调用 `BinFloat::*_ctx` 并显式携带 tuple。"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float_checked.md:54
msgid "Use the wrapper for first-error pipelines, not for status accumulation."
msgstr "用它表达 first-error，而不是 status accumulation。"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float_checked.md:55
msgid "Keep all operands wrapped when using binary combinators."
msgstr "Binary combinator 的 operand 均保持 wrapped。"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float_checked.md:56
msgid "Extract once at an application boundary rather than repeatedly unwrapping."
msgstr "只在外部边界提取一次。"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float_checked.md:57
msgid "Use raw `bin_float` context APIs when rounding flags or interchange bits are required."
msgstr "需要 flags/interchange 时使用原始 `bin_float` API。"

#: manual/tutorial/bin_float_checked.md:60
msgid "See [Design](../design/bin_float_checked.md) for the state model and [`bin_float` tutorial](bin_float.md) for contexts and flags."
msgstr "参见 [Design](../design/bin_float_checked.md) 与 [`bin_float` 教程](bin_float.md)。"

